1) No period from January 22nd to 24th, 1996, there was no extraordinary movement of vehicles of any type, but on January 25th and 26th, 1996, when trucks were dispatched to VARGINHA-MG to be serviced at the Mercedes-Benz dealership, AUTOMACO, as per Commitment Note No. 96NEQ0033 of January 23rd, 1996, and Fiscal Note No. 003788 of January 29th, 1996, from the AUTOMACO company (pages 437-44), the Vehicle Outbound Control Logs of the Guard Corps (pages 53-57), and witness statements;

2) The team that transported the trucks consisted of FC ORLANDO and Captains VASSALO and WELBER on January 25th and 26th, in the morning, as per their statements on pages (10, 23-24) and, on the afternoon of the 26th, by FC ORLANDO, CbDAVID, and Sd DE MELO, as per documents and statements (pages 26-27);

3) Sd CIRILO did not participate in any convoy of trucks that traveled to VARGINHA-MG, according to the testimony of the military themselves (page 12) and FC ORLANDO (page 23).
